  "description": "Compares the cost of maintenance activities to the revenue lost during downtime for those repairs.",
  "definition": "A ratio indicating the financial efficiency of maintenance, calculated as $R_{M/R} = \\frac{\\text{Total Maintenance Cost}}{\\text{Total Revenue Loss}}$. A value < 1 suggests that the cost of repair was less than the revenue saved by returning the system to operation."
